course: dictionary
lesson: 15242
title: Sheathed: covered or put away
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words can mean more than one thing, and the words around them show you which meaning to use. Sheathed is one of these words. Always read the whole sentence before you decide.
explain: «The knight sheathed his sword and smiled at his friend.» The fight is over, so sheathed means the sword was put back into its cover. Sheathe is the verb, and sheathed is its past form.
explain: «The cable was sheathed in plastic to keep out the water.» Here sheathed is an adjective. It means covered or wrapped in a close-fitting layer. Ask: what is the layer for? It protects the cable. Try your meaning in the sentence to check that it makes sense.
fact: Sheathe means to put a knife or sword back into its cover.
fact: «Sheathed» means covered or wrapped in a close-fitting layer, as in «steel-sheathed» or «sheathed in ice».
fact: «Sheathed» can also describe a cat's claws that are pulled back in and not showing.
fact: In stories, «he sheathed his sword» can mean the fight is over or that he chose peace.
fact: In science and design, things are sheathed in a protective layer, like cables sheathed in plastic.
exercise: «The soldier sheathed his sword and walked home.» What does sheathed mean here? | Sharpened on a stone | Thrown across the field | *Put back into its cover | Lost in the mud
exercise: «The cable was sheathed in plastic to keep out the water.» What does sheathed mean here? | Cut into two pieces | Hidden under the sand | *Covered in a protective layer | Painted bright red
exercise: Mia says, «The cat's claws were sheathed.» What does that mean? | *Pulled back in and not showing | Coloured black | Very long and curved | Sharp and showing
test: What does «sheathed» suggest about the fight in «The knight sheathed his sword after the battle ended»? | *The fight was over | The knight lost his sword | The fight had just started | The battle was on the moon
test: «The trees were sheathed in ice after the storm.» What does sheathed mean? | Cut down by the wind | Melted into water | Painted white | *Covered in a close-fitting layer
exam: In «The ship's hull was sheathed in copper to protect it from the sea», which word means covered or wrapped in a layer? | ship | *sheathed | hull | copper
